# Series 02 - RStudio

This repository contains my work for **Section 2 of Series 02** of the RStudio course.

The main topic of this section is **Statistical Tests**, including the comparison of medians and means using parametric and non-parametric tests.

## Teamwork and Document Structure

The project uses a **master Quarto document** together with several **sub-documents**.

The sub-documents are used so that different contributors can **work on different sections simultaneously** without having to edit the same file at the same time. The master document includes all the sub-documents and combines them into one document when it is rendered.

### Section 2.1: Statistical Tests

This section covers the basic concepts needed to understand statistical tests:

* Mean and median
* Variance and standard deviation
* Normal distribution
* Statistical tests
* Parametric and non-parametric tests
* Assumptions of statistical tests
* P-values
* Type I and Type II errors
* Paired and unpaired tests

**File:** `section_2.1.qmd`

### Section 2.2: Effect of Treatment Over Time

This section analyzes before-and-after measurements to investigate the effect of rehabilitation training over time.

#### 2.2.1: The Data

This part describes the measured variables, including:

* Variable descriptions
* Units
* Possible values
* Expected changes after rehabilitation

**File:** `section_2.2.1.qmd`

#### 2.2.2: The Analysis

This part focuses on:

* Testing whether the treatment has an effect
* Choosing an appropriate statistical test
* Choosing a graph to illustrate the effect
* Writing a result sentence

**File:** `section_2.2.2.qmd`

### Section 2.3: Testing Some Stereotypes

This section uses anthropometric and qualitative data to investigate different stereotypes about snoring and other characteristics.

#### 2.3.1: The Data

This part introduces and describes the `snore.txt` dataset.

**File:** `section_2.3.1.qmd`

#### 2.3.2: The Analysis

This part investigates:

* Whether snorers are fatter
* Whether snorers drink or smoke more
* Whether men are fatter
* Whether women smoke less
* Correlations between variables

**File:** `section_2.3.2.qmd`

